#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:46
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:48
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&knewsticker; is an applet for the &kde; panel (also known as &kicker;) "
"which provides an easy and convenient way to access the news as reported by "
"many news sites (such as <ulink url=\"http://slashdot.org\">Slashdot</"
"ulink>, <ulink url=\"http://lwn.net\">&Linux; Weekly News</ulink> or <ulink "
"url=\"http://freshmeat.net\">Freshmeat</ulink>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To achieve this, &knewsticker; requires the news sites to provide a special "
"&RSS; file, which contains the headlines as well as pointers to the "
"corresponding full articles. Such files are very common these days, and "
"&knewsticker; already comes with a selection of good news sources which "
"provide such files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid "Brief Info On &RSS; Files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:63
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&RSS; files are becoming more and more popular these days, and this applet "
"is not the first application which takes advantage of them. But what are "
"&RSS; files? This section tries to give a brief answer to this question, as "
"well as pointers to other sources for further reference."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The short answer: &RSS; is an <acronym>&XML;-based</acronym> format for "
"syndicating web content."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:72
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&RSS; is often used as an acronym for <quote>Rich Site Summary</quote> "
"&ndash; that's not a common definition but it gives an idea on what the "
"creators of &RSS; had in mind. There is no consensus on what &RSS; stands "
"for, so it's actually not an acronym, it's a name."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&RSS; originated in 1999 and was invented by <ulink url=\"http://www."
"netscape.com\">NetScape</ulink> as a syndication format for their <ulink url="
"\"http://my.netscape.com\">my.netscape.com</ulink> website; this very first "
"&RSS; release was version 0.9. A few months after that, &Netscape; "
"introduced &RSS; version 0.91, which incorporated many features of the "
"<quote>&lt;scriptingNews&gt;</quote> format."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The basic concept of all &RSS; files is to provide a clean, simple and "
"portable way to distribute web content, in particular news: the news sites "
"provide an &RSS; file which basically contains a set of records, and each "
"record consists of a headline and a &URL; which points to the complete "
"article. The &RSS; file also contains other general information about the "
"particular news site, such as its name and the homepage, which is evaluated "
"by &knewsticker;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Nowadays there are a few additional, more sophisticated versions of the "
"&RSS; format (<ulink url=\"http://backend.userland.com/rss091\">0.91</"
"ulink>, <ulink url=\"http://backend.userland.com/rss092\">0.92</ulink>, "
"<ulink url=\"http://backend.userland.com/rss093\">0.93</ulink>, <ulink url="
"\"http://web.resource.org/rss/1.0/\">1.0</ulink> and the current format "
"version <ulink url=\"http://backend.userland.com/rss\">2.0</ulink>) but the "
"first two versions still make up about 85% of the files provided on the web. "
"Nevertheless, all versions up to 2.0 can be processed with &knewsticker;!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Of course, this is only a short and highly incomplete attempt at explaining "
"the basic ideas behind &RSS; files. If you're interested in this topic, you "
"might want to visit any of the following links which point to further and "
"more complete sources on this:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: ulink
#: index.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid "http://www.webreference.com/authoring/languages/xml/rss/intro/"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A very pragmatic introduction to the &RSS; format, with concrete examples "
"and guidelines. Together with the authoritative specifications, this makes a "
"good guide for people who are thinking about providing an &RSS; newsfeed on "
"their home page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: ulink
#: index.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid "http://www.oreillynet.com/rss/"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:123
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &RSS; page from O'Reilly features a lot of general articles about "
"employing and using &RSS; files, up to date news about the &RSS; development "
"community as well as vital information for web developers who are "
"considering taking advantage of &RSS;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: ulink
#: index.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid "http://blogspace.com/rss/"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This page is another excellent source of news about the &RSS; development, "
"which is especially interesting to developers working with &RSS;-based "
"technology."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: ulink
#: index.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid "http://www.w3.org/RDF/"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<emphasis>The</emphasis> authoritative source about <acronym>RDF</acronym>, "
"an &XML;-based language from which modern &RSS; versions are derived, "
"published by the <ulink url=\"http://www.w3.org\">World Wide Web Consortium</"
"ulink>. It features a comprehensive list of links to other sites on the "
"topic as well as a timeline of the <acronym>RDF</acronym> development, an "
"overview over the architecture, an archive with articles about <acronym>RDF</"
"acronym> as well as a carefully assembled list of tools for developers who "
"intend to work with <acronym>RDF</acronym>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:149
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Developers will also want to check the authoritative specifications for the "
"various &RSS; versions:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:153
#, no-c-format
msgid "&RSS; Specifications"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:154
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Version 0.90: <ulink url=\"http://www.purplepages.ie/rss/netscape/rss0.90."
"html\">http://www.purplepages.ie/rss/netscape/rss0.90.html</ulink>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:157
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Version 0.91: <ulink url=\"http://backend.userland.com/rss091\">http://"
"backend.userland.com/rss091</ulink>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:160
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Version 0.92: <ulink url=\"http://backend.userland.com/rss092\">http://"
"backend.userland.com/rss092</ulink>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:163
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Version 0.93: <ulink url=\"http://backend.userland.com/rss093\">http://"
"backend.userland.com/rss093</ulink>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:166
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Version 1.0: <ulink url=\"http://web.resource.org/rss/1.0/\">http://web."
"resource.org/rss/1.0/</ulink>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:169
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Version 2.0: <ulink url=\"http://backend.userland.com/rss\">http://backend."
"userland.com/rss</ulink>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:174
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you find any other sites or documents on this topic, and think they are "
"worth being mentioned here, don't hesitate to send them to &Frerich.Raabe; "
"&Frerich.Raabe.mail; so that they can be included in this document and help "
"everybody."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:179
#, no-c-format
msgid "Thank you very much!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid "Starting &knewsticker;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:187
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>Here is a screenshot of &knewsticker; in &kde;'s panel.</"
"screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:192
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Here is a screenshot of &knewsticker; in &kde;'s panel.</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:198
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&knewsticker; is started like every other &kicker; applet. You just have to "
"add it to the panel (or any child panel of the main one). To do so, just "
"right-click on the &kde; panel and choose <guimenuitem>Add Applet to Panel..."
"</guimenuitem> and <guilabel>News Ticker</guilabel> in the dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:205
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>Here is a screenshot of &knewsticker; in its own child panel.</"
"screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:210
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<phrase>Here is a screenshot of &knewsticker; in its own child panel.</"
"phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:216
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Another good way to use &knewsticker; is to put it into its own child panel. "
"Just add a new child panel by choosing <menuchoice> <guimenu>New Panel</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Panel</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> from the panel menu;. "
"Now you can simply right-click on the child panel and select &knewsticker; "
"as described above."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:223
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>Here is a screenshot of &knewsticker; in its own window.</"
"screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:228
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Here is a screenshot of &knewsticker; in its own window.</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:234
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A third, popular, way to run &knewsticker; is by selecting <menuchoice> "
"<guimenu>Internet</guimenu><guisubmenu>More Applications</"
"guisubmenu><guimenuitem>&knewsticker; (News Ticker)</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice> from the <guilabel>K</guilabel> menu. This will start "
"&knewsticker; and make it run in its own window which you can then resize "
"and move around as you wish."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:242
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring &knewsticker;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:244
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can access &knewsticker;'s configuration dialog by right-clicking onto "
"the scroll text, or by clicking on the button with the arrow on it and "
"choosing the entry labelled <guimenuitem><inlinemediaobject><imageobject> "
"<imagedata fileref=\"preferences-icon.png\" format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject> </"
"inlinemediaobject> Preferences</guimenuitem> in the menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:251
#, no-c-format
msgid "General Options"
msgstr "Opcions generalas"

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:254
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>This is what the <guilabel>General</guilabel> tab of the "
"preferences dialog looks like.</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:259
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<phrase>This is what the <guilabel>General</guilabel> tab of the preferences "
"dialog looks like.</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:265
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can define how fast the text should be scrolled around, what it "
"should look like as well as other options for the applet. Here is a brief "
"info on what each of the switches and buttons on this tab does:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:271
#, no-c-format
msgid "Mousewheel sensitivity:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:273
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This slider allows you to define how fast/slow the text should be scrolled "
"when using the mousewheel."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:278
#, no-c-format
msgid "News query interval"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:280
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can define in what intervals &knewsticker; queries the configured "
"news sources for new headlines. This depends generally on how fast you'd "
"like to hear about news and how much load you want to put on the network:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:286
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A lower value (lower than 15 minutes) enables you to be notified about news "
"very quickly if you want or need to. Please note, that it increases the "
"network traffic significantly, though. Therefore, such low values shouldn't "
"be used if you query popular news sites (such as <ulink url=\"http://"
"slashdot.org\">Slashdot</ulink> or <ulink url=\"http://freshmeat.net"
"\">Freshmeat</ulink>) as they have generally already enough work with "
"processing the incoming queries."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:297
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A higher value (higher than 45 minutes) won't make you hear about news that "
"quick. For non-time-critical applications, it should be suitable, though. "
"The positive aspect of longer intervals is that only very little load is put "
"on the network; this saves resources and nerves, for you and the system "
"administrators of the news sites you query."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:305
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The default value (30 minutes) should be appropriate and reasonable in most "
"cases."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:310
#, no-c-format
msgid "Use custom names for news sites"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:312
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Check this box to make the news ticker use the names you specified in the "
"list of news sources (available on the tab labeled <guilabel>News sources</"
"guilabel>) instead of the ones the news sites themselves report. This can be "
"handy for news sites which report a very long or useless name."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:323
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuration of the news sources"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:326
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>This is what the <guilabel>News Sources</guilabel> tab of the "
"preferences dialog looks like.</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:331
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<phrase>This is what the <guilabel>News Sources</guilabel> tab of the "
"preferences dialog looks like.</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:337
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On this tab you can manage and maintain the list of news sites &knewsticker; "
"queries for news. Click on any entry with the right mouse button to open a "
"context menu which lets you remove the current entry, or add a new entry. At "
"the bottom of the page you can also find three buttons which have the same "
"effect."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:344
#, no-c-format
msgid "Adding a news site"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:345
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are four ways to <emphasis>add</emphasis> a new news site to the list:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:349
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can click on the button at the bottom labeled <guilabel>Add...</"
"guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:353
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can click with the right mouse button on the table and choose "
"<guimenuitem>Add news source</guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:357
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can drag any &RSS; file from another application (such as &konqueror;) "
"onto the table. This adds a new entry to the list, sets the name to "
"<quote>Unknown</quote> and sets the maximum number of articles to 10."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:363
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"And finally, you can just click on any &RSS; file in the &konqueror; "
"filemanager to have it added to the list immediately."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:368
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Either way will cause the <link linkend=\"config-news-site-dialog\">News "
"site dialog</link> to show up, presenting you with a form to enter the "
"properties of the news site to add."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:374
#, no-c-format
msgid "Modifying an existing news site"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:375
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are two ways to adjust the properties of an existing news site:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:379
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can click on the button at the bottom labeled <guilabel>Modify...</"
"guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:383
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can right-click with the right mouse button on the news site you'd like "
"to edit and choose <guimenuitem>Modify '...'</guimenuitem> from the menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:388
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"No matter which way you chose, it will cause the <link linkend=\"config-news-"
"site-dialog\">News site dialog</link> to pop up, showing the properties of "
"the selected news site."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:394
#, no-c-format
msgid "Removing a news site"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:395
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Of course, you want to <emphasis>remove</emphasis> a news source from the "
"list sometimes. To do this, you can either"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:399
#, no-c-format
msgid "click on the button at the bottom labeled <guilabel>Remove</guilabel>, or"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:403
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"right-click with the right mouse button on the news site you'd like to edit "
"and choose <guimenuitem>Remove '...'</guimenuitem> from the menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:408
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In both cases, a confirmation box will pop up and make sure you didn't "
"select the wrong entry."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:410
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can also remove multiple news sites at once by holding &Ctrl; while "
"clicking on the entries you wouldd like to remove, or by clicking the "
"<mousebutton>left</mousebutton> mousebutton and dragging the mouse over all "
"the entries you'd like to select."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:417
#, no-c-format
msgid "The news site dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:420
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>This is what the dialog for adding and editing news sites looks "
"like.</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:425
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<phrase>This is what the dialog for adding and editing news sites looks like."
"</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:431
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When adding or modifying a news site, the news site dialog (shown above) "
"pops up and provides input facilities to edit the various properties of a "
"news site:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:437
#, no-c-format
msgid "Name:"
msgstr "Nom :"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:439
#, no-c-format
msgid "This is the name of the news source."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:440
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This text will only be used if <guilabel>Use custom names for news sites</"
"guilabel> on the tab labeled <link linkend=\"config-general\">General</link> "
"is activated."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:447
#, no-c-format
msgid "Source file:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:449
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can set the &URL; which references the &RSS; file of this news "
"site; this can either be a local file, or a file saved on a remote server. "
"You can also click on the button at the right to open a convenient file-"
"selection dialog and browse to the file you would like to use, instead of "
"typing the &URL; by hand."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:458
#, no-c-format
msgid "The file is a program"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:460
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this file is checked, &knewsticker; will not assume that the &URL; (which "
"was specified in the <guilabel>Source file</guilabel> field) references an "
"&RSS; file, but rather that the &URL; refers a program (usually a script). "
"When querying this news site, &knewsticker; will execute the program and "
"treat whatever the program prints to stdout as &RSS; markup. This is very "
"convenient for conversion scripts which download an &HTML; file and process "
"it, producing &RSS; markup which is suitable for use with &knewsticker;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:470
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can find some scripts which &eg; download stock data in the kdeaddons "
"module, in the <filename class=\"directory\">knewsticker-scripts</filename> "
"directory."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:477
#, no-c-format
msgid "Category:"
msgstr "Categoria :"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:479
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can specify into which category the news site belongs. Arranging "
"the news sites into categories makes it much easier to maintain large lists "
"of news sites."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:485
#, no-c-format
msgid "Max. articles:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:487
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This option lets you define how many articles &knewsticker; will cache for "
"this news site; the value will never be exceeded."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:489
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is particularly handy for news sites which provide only three news "
"items at once, but you'd like to see the last ten items (for instance); "
"&knewsticker; will always download the three items and merge them into its "
"list, caching the last seven items."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:496
#, no-c-format
msgid "Icon:"
msgstr "Icòna :"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:498
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can specify a &URL; to an image file (preferably 16x16 pixels in "
"size) which should be used for this news site. Icons make it much easier to "
"distinguish multiple news sites, and see which news site a headline appeared "
"on as it scrolls by in &knewsticker;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:507
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"At the button you will find the usual buttons. One of them deserves an extra "
"note: clicking on the <guilabel>Suggest</guilabel> button will make "
"&knewsticker; try to guess suitable values for most of the fields if you "
"specify a &URL; to a valid source file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:512
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This means that you can usually just paste a &URL; to an &RSS; file in the "
"input field labeled <guilabel>Source file</guilabel>, press the "
"<guilabel>Suggest</guilabel> button and then modify the suggested values as "
"needed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:520
#, no-c-format
msgid "Filters"
msgstr "Filtres"

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:523
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>This is what the <guilabel>Filters</guilabel> tab of the "
"preferences dialog looks like.</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:528
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<phrase>This is what the <guilabel>Filters</guilabel> tab of the preferences "
"dialog looks like.</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:534
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This tab allows you to define various filters which should be applied before "
"showing the headlines in the scroll text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:537
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These filters only affect the headlines which are shown in the scrolltext; "
"the menu will always show all of the headlines."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:539
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The major part of the tab is occupied by a table which lists the currently "
"configured filters. Each filter has a small checkable box - checking that "
"box enables the filter, unchecking it temporarily disables it without "
"removing it from the list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:544
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By default there are no filters, so chances are that the table is completely "
"empty for you. Of course, this dialog provides you with ways to add new "
"filters, and manage them in general:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:550
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To <emphasis>add</emphasis> a filter, simply enter the filter properties "
"(see <link linkend=\"filter-components\">Filter Components</link> for a "
"detailed description of the various filter properties) using the input "
"fields in the box labeled <guilabel>Filter properties</guilabel> and then "
"press the button labeled <guilabel>Add</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:558
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To <emphasis>modify</emphasis> an existing filter, select the filter you "
"would like to edit in the table by left-clicking on it and then change its "
"properties in the box at the bottom."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:563
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To <emphasis>remove</emphasis> a filter, select it in the table and then "
"press the button labeled <guilabel>Remove</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:569 index.docbook:574
#, no-c-format
msgid "Filter Components"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:571
#, no-c-format
msgid "Each filter consists of four components:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:576
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Action &ndash; this can be either <guilabel>Show</guilabel> or "
"<guilabel>Hide</guilabel> and defines what should happen to a headline in "
"case this filter matches."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:581
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"News sources &ndash; here you can define whether the filter affects only "
"single news sources, or whether this filter should be applied to the "
"headlines of all news sources."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:586
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Condition &ndash; this is a verb which defines, together with the "
"Expression, whether a filter matches. A condition can be &eg; "
"<guilabel>contains</guilabel>, <guilabel>doesn't equal</guilabel> or "
"<guilabel>matches</guilabel>. See below for a more detailed description."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:593
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Expression - this is a user-defined string which forms the body of the "
"filter, together with the Condition. See below for a more detailed "
"description of this component."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:599
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All these components can be configured using the facilities in the frame "
"labeled <guilabel>Filter properties</guilabel>. The possible states of the "
"Condition component deserve a special explanation:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:605
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>contains</guilabel>, <guilabel>doesn't contain</guilabel>: this "
"filter matches if the headline contains / doesn't contain the specified "
"expression."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:608
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The expression isn't treated case-sensitively, so the expressions "
"<quote>KDE</quote>, <quote>kDE</quote> or <quote>kde</quote> will all match "
"headlines which contain <quote>KDE</quote>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:613
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>equals</guilabel>, <guilabel>doesn't equal</guilabel>: this filter "
"matches if the headline equals / doesn't equal the specified expression."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:616
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The expression is treated case-sensitively, so of the expressions "
"<quote>&Linux;</quote>, <quote>linux</quote> or <quote>LINUX</quote>, only "
"the first will match <quote>&Linux;</quote>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:621
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>matches</guilabel>: using this condition will make &knewsticker; "
"treat the given expression as a <quote>regular expression</quote>. For "
"further information on regular expressions you might want to read <ulink url="
"\"http://www.evolt.org/article/rating/20/22700/\">this article</ulink> which "
"was published at <ulink url=\"http://www.evolt.org\">www.evolt.org</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:634
#, no-c-format
msgid "Scroller Preferences"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:637
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>This is what the <guilabel>Scroller Preferences</guilabel> tab "
"of the preferences dialog looks like.</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:642
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<phrase>This is what the <guilabel>Scroller Preferences</guilabel> tab of "
"the preferences dialog looks like.</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:648
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This tab lets you define various options which affect &knewsticker;'s scroll "
"text:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:653
#, no-c-format
msgid "Scrolling speed"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:655
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This slider lets you define how fast the scrolltext should be scrolling. If "
"you have rather little space on your taskbar (and therefore a rather small "
"news ticker), you should probably set this to a lower value so that you have "
"a chance to read the headlines. For wider news tickers (and better eyes), a "
"faster text is probably appropriate so that you have to wait for the next "
"headline only as little as possible."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:665
#, no-c-format
msgid "Direction of scrolling"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:667
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These options allow you to define in what direction the text should be "
"scrolled, &eg; to the left or to the right, upwards or downwards. You can "
"also rotate the text by 90 or 270 degrees here, which is not exactly "
"readable but it makes sense for vertically aligned panels."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:675
#, no-c-format
msgid "Scrolltext font"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:677
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click on the button at the right labeled <guilabel>Choose Font...</guilabel> "
"to choose the font which will be used for the scrolling text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:680
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Certain fonts are harder to read than others, especially when they are used "
"for a scrolltext, so you should probably choose a font which can even easily "
"be read if it's moving."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:686
#, no-c-format
msgid "Foreground color"
msgstr "Color de _fons"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:688
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click this button open a convenient color-selection dialog which lets you "
"choose the color which will be used for the foreground of the scrolling text "
"(&ie; the color of the text itself)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:694
#, no-c-format
msgid "Background color"
msgstr "Color de fons"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:696
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click this button to open a convenient color-selection dialog which lets you "
"choose the color which will be used for the background of the scrolling text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:702
#, no-c-format
msgid "Highlighted color"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:704
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click this button to open a convenient color-selection dialog which lets you "
"choose the color which will be used for the color of the headlines when they "
"are highlighted (when you move the mouse over them)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:711
#, no-c-format
msgid "Scroll the most recent headlines only"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:713
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Check this button to make the scrolltext show just the most recent headline "
"for each news site, instead of showing every headline available from every "
"news site."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:719
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show icons"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:721
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Checking this box will make &knewsticker; show an icon (if available) in "
"front of each headline which is scrolled along; this makes determining which "
"news site provided each headline much easier."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:728
#, no-c-format
msgid "Temporarily slowed scrolling"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:730
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Check this box to make &knewsticker; slow the scrolling down when you move "
"the mouse cursor over the scrolling text. This makes clicking on items and "
"dragging away the icons (if enabled) a lot easier."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:737
#, no-c-format
msgid "Underline highlighted headline"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:739
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Check this box to have the currently highlighted headline (&ie; the headline "
"which is currently under the mouse cursor) underlined."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:749
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &knewsticker;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:751
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using &knewsticker; is fairly straightforward and should give you no big "
"problems, assuming that you have already <link linkend=\"configuration"
"\">configured it</link>. No matter whether you are running &knewsticker; in "
"the main panel, in its own child panel or in its own window, it appears as "
"an area with a scrolling text and a button with a small arrow next to it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:759
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Main Interface"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:761
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The area (it is white by default, but you can change the background color "
"easily using the preferences dialog) with the scrolling text in it is called "
"the <quote>news scroller</quote>. It keeps scrolling the downloaded "
"headlines (or just the most recent headlines) continuously and provides easy "
"access to the articles. If you see an interesting article, just click on it "
"to open the &konqueror; web browser, showing the full article which belongs "
"to the headline you clicked on. If you feel that a possibly interesting "
"headline just scrolled out of view, you have some ways to influence the "
"scrolling:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:773
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can click on the news scroller with the <mousebutton>left</mousebutton> "
"mouse button and move the mouse around (while holding the <mousebutton>left</"
"mousebutton> mouse button pressed down). The news scroller will continue "
"scrolling as usual if you release the left mouse button again."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:780
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you own a so-called <quote>wheel mouse</quote>, you can use the wheel on "
"your mouse to scroll the headlines back and forth."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:785
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There's also a very powerful <link linkend=\"contextmenu-descr\">context "
"menu</link>, which you can access either by clicking on the news scroller "
"with the <mousebutton>right</mousebutton> mouse button, or by clicking on "
"the arrow button with the <mousebutton>left</mousebutton> button. This "
"context menu is the most interesting part of the applet, as it contains "
"about all the functionality."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:794
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Context Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:797
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>This is what the context menu of &knewsticker; looks like, when "
"using just the default news sites.</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:802
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<phrase>This is what the context menu of &knewsticker; looks like, when "
"using just the default news sites.</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:808
#, no-c-format
msgid "The context menu is basically split into two functional parts:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:810
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The upper part shows a list of entries, each entry having a small icon like "
"this <inlinemediaobject><imageobject> <imagedata fileref=\"newssite-icon.png"
"\" format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject> </inlinemediaobject> next to it. This list "
"represents the list of currently configured news sites. You can click on any "
"of the news sources to open another menu which contains a listing of "
"headlines which are available for that particular news site as well as an "
"entry labeled <guilabel> <inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref="
"\"checknews-icon.png\" format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject> "
"Check news</guilabel> to refresh the headline list for this news site. Each "
"of the headlines has an <inlinemediaobject><imageobject> <imagedata fileref="
"\"oldarticle-icon.png\" format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject> </inlinemediaobject> "
"icon next to it indicating that that you have read that article already or "
"the <inlinemediaobject><imageobject> <imagedata fileref=\"newarticle-icon.png"
"\" format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject> </inlinemediaobject> if it is still unread."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:828
#, no-c-format
msgid "The lower part currently shows five entries (explained from top to bottom):"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:833
#, no-c-format
msgid "Check news"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:835
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This entry has a little <inlinemediaobject><imageobject> <imagedata fileref="
"\"checknews-icon.png\" format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject> </inlinemediaobject> "
"next to it. If you want to force &knewsticker; to check the configured news "
"sites for new articles, you can click here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:840
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This does not reset the internal timer which queries the news sites for new "
"headlines automatically in certain intervals."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:846
#, no-c-format
msgid "Offline mode"
msgstr "Mòde sens connexion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:848
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This entry in the context menu has no icon associated with it. Click this "
"button to enable a special <quote>offline mode</quote> which pauses the "
"internal timer for querying the news sites and prevents any automatic "
"download of new headlines. The offline mode comes in handy if you have to "
"leave your computer for a while during which the system isn't connected to "
"the Internet, as it saves you from all the error messages which pop up if "
"any of the news sites couldn't be connected."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:856
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can still force a reload for single news sites as well as for all the "
"news sites by selecting the respective "
"<guilabel><inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"checknews-"
"icon.png\" format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject> </inlinemediaobject> Check news</"
"guilabel> entry."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:864
#, no-c-format
msgid "Help"
msgstr "Ajuda"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:866
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This entry is marked with a small <inlinemediaobject> "
"<imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"help-icon.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> </"
"imageobject></inlinemediaobject>. Clicking on this entry opens the "
"&knewsticker; documentation (which you're reading in this moment) which "
"details all the features and abilities of &knewsticker;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:875
#, no-c-format
msgid "About"
msgstr "A prepaus de"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:877
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This entry is marked with a small <inlinemediaobject> "
"<imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"knewsticker-icon.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> </"
"imageobject></inlinemediaobject>. Clicking on this entry opens a small "
"dialog showing who's to blame for &knewsticker; and credits people who "
"contributed significant enhancements for it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:886
#, no-c-format
msgid "Preferences"
msgstr "Preferéncias"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:888
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This entry is easily recognizable due to the <inlinemediaobject> "
"<imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"preferences-icon.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> </"
"imageobject></inlinemediaobject> icon which is next to it. Select this entry "
"to open the <link linkend=\"configuration\">preferences dialog</link> which "
"lets you customize all of the properties of &knewsticker;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:902
#, no-c-format
msgid "Frequently Asked Questions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: chapter
#: index.docbook:902
#, no-c-format
msgid "&reporting.bugs;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:909
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where do I find the &RSS; file for the news site XYZ?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:913
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It's possible that the news site you're referring to doesn't provide any "
"&RSS; file at all! Here's a short list of websites which provide thousands "
"of &RSS; feeds, sorted by language and/or topic - for free:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: ulink
#: index.docbook:920
#, no-c-format
msgid "WebReference.com"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: ulink
#: index.docbook:923
#, no-c-format
msgid "NewsIsFree"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: ulink
#: index.docbook:926
#, no-c-format
msgid "MoreOver"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:930
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have found any interesting news sites which provide such a backend, "
"don't hesitate to send them to &Frerich.Raabe; &Frerich.Raabe.mail; so that "
"they can be included in future releases. Thank you!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:938
#, no-c-format
msgid "How can I make &knewsticker; open articles in another browser (&eg; Mozilla)?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:942
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&knewsticker; will use whatever browser you have associated with the text/"
"html &MIME; type; the default browser used for viewing &HTML; pages is "
"&konqueror;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:945
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can find the dialog for changing this association by opening the &kde; "
"control center and browsing to <menuchoice><guimenu>KDE Components</guimenu> "
"<guisubmenu>File Associations</guisubmenu></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

