#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:985
#, no-c-format
msgid "Glossary"
msgstr "Glossari"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:987
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This chapter is intended to explain the various acronyms which have been "
"used throughout the &knewsticker; documentation. If you feel any acronyms or "
"terms are missing here, please don't hesitate to send an email to &Frerich."
"Raabe; &Frerich.Raabe.mail; so that they can be added. Thank you!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: glossterm
#: index.docbook:993
#, no-c-format
msgid "<glossterm>RDF</glossterm>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:995
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Resource Description Framework. A language derived from &XML; which "
"describes metadata. Commonly used as a backend format for articles and other "
"publications. For more detailed information on <acronym>RDF</acronym> files, "
"you might want to go directly to the <ulink url=\"http://www.w3.org/RDF/"
"\">official page on <acronym>RDF</acronym> files</ulink> at the <ulink url="
"\"http://www.w3.org\">World Wide Web Consortium</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: glossterm
#: index.docbook:1006
#, no-c-format
msgid "&RSS;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1008
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <acronym>RDF</acronym> Site Summary is actually an extension to the "
"<acronym>RDF</acronym> language. Quoting the official <ulink url=\"http://"
"www.purl.org/rss/1.0/\">&RSS; v1.0 specification</ulink>:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: quote
#: index.docbook:1012
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<acronym>RDF</acronym> Site Summary (&RSS;) is a lightweight multipurpose "
"extensible metadata description and syndication format. &RSS; is an &XML; "
"application, conforms to the <acronym>W3C</acronym>'s <acronym>RDF</acronym> "
"specification and is extensible via &XML;-namespace and/or <acronym>RDF</"
"acronym> based modularization."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: glossterm
#: index.docbook:1022
#, no-c-format
msgid "&XML;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1024
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Extensible Markup Language is the <quote>universal format for structured "
"documents and data on the Web</quote>. It's a derivative of <acronym>SGML</"
"acronym> which fits the needs of the world wide web. You might want to check "
"the the <ulink url=\"http://www.w3.org/XML/\">Extensible Markup Language</"
"ulink> page at the <ulink url=\"http://www.w3.org\">World Wide Web "
"Consortium</ulink> for further information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: glossterm
#: index.docbook:1034
#, no-c-format
msgid "<glossterm>W3C</glossterm>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1036
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"An abbreviation for <quote>World Wide Web Consortium</quote>. Quoting the "
"<ulink url=\"http://www.w3.org\">official homepage</ulink> of the "
"<acronym>W3C</acronym>, <quote>the World Wide Web Consortium (<acronym>W3C</"
"acronym>) develops interoperable technologies (specifications, guidelines, "
"software, and tools) to lead the Web to its full potential as a forum for "
"information, commerce, communication, and collective understanding</quote>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: glossterm
#: index.docbook:1046
#, no-c-format
msgid "&URL;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1048
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&URL; stands for <quote>Uniform Resource Locator</quote>, a specially "
"formatted string which can reference resources like images, documents and "
"other things on the Internet. Please refer to the corresponding <ulink url="
"\"http://www.w3.org/Addressing/\">webpage</ulink> for more detailed "
"information on this topic."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: glossterm
#: index.docbook:1056
#, no-c-format
msgid "&DCOP;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1058
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Desktop COmmunication Protocol is a way for applications to communicate "
"to each other. For instance, &knewsticker;'s <link linkend=\"configuration"
"\">configuration dialog</link> uses &DCOP; to tell the applet itself about "
"the current configuration."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1063
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&knewsticker; provides an extensive <link linkend=\"develinfo\">&DCOP; "
"interface</link>, which makes it possible to control many of &knewsticker;'s "
"functions from the commandline."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1067
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more detailled information on &DCOP; you might want to visit <ulink url="
"\"http://developer.kde.org/documentation/library/2.0-api/dcop/HOWTO.html"
"\">http://developer.kde.org/documentation/library/2.0-api/dcop/HOWTO.html</"
"ulink> for a complete explanation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1076
#, no-c-format
msgid "Information For Developers And Advanced Users"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1078
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&knewsticker; features a currently rather extensive, and steadily growing "
"&DCOP; interface. This is not only used to communicate with other "
"applications, it makes it possible to control &knewsticker; with a shell "
"script as well. The more the interface is extended, the more useful it will "
"become and the more flexible &knewsticker; will be controllable from a "
"script."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1085
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To use these &DCOP; functions you can either use the <application>dcop</"
"application> commandline program or use the more convenient "
"<application>KDCOP</application> application. Both provide the same "
"functionality so it's actually just a matter of taste which program you "
"prefer. :-)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1091
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This chapter assumes that you're using the commandline program "
"<application>dcop</application>. To access &knewsticker;'s &DCOP; functions "
"make sure that &knewsticker; is <link linkend=\"starting-knewsticker"
"\">started</link> and then just enter something like this at the console:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:1097
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>dcop</command> <option>knewsticker</"
"option> <option>KNewsTicker</option> <option>[function]</option></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1099
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If an error appears that tells you that <filename>dcop</filename> couldn't "
"be found or executed, please check whether the file <filename>dcop</"
"filename> exists in <filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/"
"bin</filename> and make sure its permissions are set appropriately."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1105
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In that command line, just replace <quote>[function]</quote> with the "
"appropriate function name, &ie; type"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:1108 index.docbook:1130
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>dcop</command> <option>knewsticker</"
"option> <option>KNewsTicker</option> <option>updateNews</option></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1110
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"to make &knewsticker; check for new news items and download them if "
"necessary."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1114
#, no-c-format
msgid "&DCOP; Reference"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1116
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this section, all methods which are accessible via &knewsticker;'s &DCOP; "
"interface are listed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: index.docbook:1121
#, no-c-format
msgid "updateNews"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1123
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function forces &knewsticker; to update the internal list of articles "
"(&ie; it queries the list of news sources which has been <link linkend="
"\"config-newssources\">configured</link> for new news) and downloads them "
"when necessary."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1127
#, no-c-format
msgid "This also works if &knewsticker; is currently in offline mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1129 index.docbook:1143 index.docbook:1154 index.docbook:1166
#: index.docbook:1175 index.docbook:1184 index.docbook:1201 index.docbook:1210
#: index.docbook:1219 index.docbook:1229 index.docbook:1238 index.docbook:1248
#: index.docbook:1258 index.docbook:1267 index.docbook:1279 index.docbook:1291
#: index.docbook:1303 index.docbook:1313
#, no-c-format
msgid "Example:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: index.docbook:1134
#, no-c-format
msgid "reparseConfig"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1136
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <command>reparseConfig</command> command makes &knewsticker; reload its "
"configuration from the configuration file. This function is used by the "
"<link linkend=\"configuration\">configuration dialog</link> to talk to "
"&knewsticker; but you can use it if you modified the configuration file by "
"hand."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1141
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The configuration file is saved in <filename>~/.kde/share/config/"
"knewsticker_appletrc</filename>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:1144
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>dcop</command> <option>knewsticker</"
"option> <option>KNewsTicker</option> <option>reparseConfig</option></"
"userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: index.docbook:1148
#, no-c-format
msgid "setOfflineMode [bool]"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1150
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can call this function to define whether &knewsticker; is currently in "
"the offline mode (&ie; whether &knewsticker; should query the <link linkend="
"\"config-newssources\">configured news sites</link> for new news)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:1155
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>dcop</command> <option>knewsticker</"
"option> <option>KNewsTicker</option> <option>setOfflineMode</option> "
"<option>true</option></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1156
#, no-c-format
msgid "to enable the offline mode, or type"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:1157
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>dcop</command> <option>knewsticker</"
"option> <option>KNewsTicker</option> <option>setOfflineMode</option> "
"<option>false</option></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1158
#, no-c-format
msgid "to disable offline mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: index.docbook:1162
#, no-c-format
msgid "interval"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1164
#, no-c-format
msgid "Returns the currently configured news query interval in minutes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:1167
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>dcop</command> <option>knewsticker</"
"option> <option>KNewsTicker</option> <option>interval</option></userinput>\n"
"                        30\n"
"                        <prompt>%</prompt>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: index.docbook:1171
#, no-c-format
msgid "scrollingSpeed"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1173
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Returns the currently configured scrolling speed. The returned scrolling "
"speed is specified in pixels per second."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:1176
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>dcop</command> <option>knewsticker</"
"option> <option>KNewsTicker</option> <option>scrollingSpeed</option></"
"userinput>\n"
"                        20\n"
"                        <prompt>%</prompt>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: index.docbook:1180
#, no-c-format
msgid "mouseWheelSpeed"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1182
#, no-c-format
msgid "Returns the number of pixels the scrolltext gets shifted per mousewheel step."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:1185
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>dcop</command> <option>knewsticker</"
"option> <option>KNewsTicker</option> <option>mouseWheelSpeed</option></"
"userinput>\n"
"                        15\n"
"                        <prompt>%</prompt>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: index.docbook:1189
#, no-c-format
msgid "scrollingDirection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1191
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Returns an integer which corresponds to the direction the scrolltext is "
"scrolling in:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1194
#, no-c-format
msgid "1 = To the left"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1195
#, no-c-format
msgid "2 = To the right"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1196
#, no-c-format
msgid "3 = Upwards"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1197
#, no-c-format
msgid "4 = Downwards"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1198
#, no-c-format
msgid "5 = Upwards, rotated"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1199
#, no-c-format
msgid "6 = Downwards, rotated"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:1202
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>dcop</command> <option>knewsticker</"
"option> <option>KNewsTicker</option> <option>scrollingDirection</option></"
"userinput>\n"
"                        1\n"
"                        <prompt>%</prompt>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: index.docbook:1206
#, no-c-format
msgid "customNames"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1208
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Returns either 'true' or 'false', depending on whether &knewsticker; uses "
"custom names for the news sites."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:1211
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>dcop</command> <option>knewsticker</"
"option> <option>KNewsTicker</option> <option>customNames</option></"
"userinput>\n"
"                        false\n"
"                        <prompt>%</prompt>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: index.docbook:1215
#, no-c-format
msgid "endlessScrolling"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1217
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Returns either 'true' or 'false', depending on whether &knewsticker; has the "
"endless scrolling option enabled."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:1220
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>dcop</command> <option>knewsticker</"
"option> <option>KNewsTicker</option> <option>endlessScrolling</option></"
"userinput>\n"
"                        true\n"
"                        <prompt>%</prompt>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: index.docbook:1224
#, no-c-format
msgid "scrollMostRecentOnly"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1226
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Returns either 'true' or 'false', depending on whether &knewsticker; "
"currently only scrolls the most recent headlines for each news site."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:1230
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>dcop</command> <option>knewsticker</"
"option> <option>KNewsTicker</option> <option>scrollMostRecentOnly</option></"
"userinput>\n"
"                        false\n"
"                        <prompt>%</prompt>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: index.docbook:1234
#, no-c-format
msgid "offlineMode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1236
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Returns either 'true' or 'false', depending on whether &knewsticker; is "
"currently in offline mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:1239
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>dcop</command> <option>knewsticker</"
"option> <option>KNewsTicker</option> <option>offlineMode</option></"
"userinput>\n"
"                        false\n"
"                        <prompt>%</prompt>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: index.docbook:1243
#, no-c-format
msgid "underlineHighlighted"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1245
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Returns either 'true' or 'false', depending on whether &knewsticker; was "
"told to underline the headline which is currently below the mouse cursor."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:1249
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>dcop</command> <option>knewsticker</"
"option> <option>KNewsTicker</option> <option>underlineHighlighted</option></"
"userinput>\n"
"                        true\n"
"                        <prompt>%</prompt>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: index.docbook:1253
#, no-c-format
msgid "showIcons"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1255
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Returns either 'true' or 'false', depending on whether &knewsticker; "
"currently shows the icon of the news site each particular headline was "
"published at in front of the headline."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:1259
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>dcop</command> <option>knewsticker</"
"option> <option>KNewsTicker</option> <option>showIcons</option></userinput>\n"
"                        true\n"
"                        <prompt>%</prompt>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: index.docbook:1263
#, no-c-format
msgid "slowedScrolling"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1265
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Returns either 'true' or 'false', depending on whether &knewsticker; has the "
"<quote>slowed scrolling</quote> feature activated."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:1268
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>dcop</command> <option>knewsticker</"
"option> <option>KNewsTicker</option> <option>slowedScrolling</option></"
"userinput>\n"
"                        false\n"
"                        <prompt>%</prompt>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: index.docbook:1272
#, no-c-format
msgid "foregroundColor"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1274
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Returns the currently configured foreground color as a string in the format "
"<quote>#rrggbb</quote>, where <quote>rr</quote>, <quote>gg</quote> and "
"<quote>bb</quote> are two-digit hexadecimal values representing the "
"intensity of the red, green and blue components in a scale of 00-ff."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:1280
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>dcop</command> <option>knewsticker</"
"option> <option>KNewsTicker</option> <option>foregroundColor</option></"
"userinput>\n"
"                        #804000\n"
"                        <prompt>%</prompt>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: index.docbook:1284
#, no-c-format
msgid "backgroundColor"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1286
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Returns the currently configured background color as a string in the format "
"<quote>#rrggbb</quote>, where <quote>rr</quote>, <quote>gg</quote> and "
"<quote>bb</quote> are two-digit hexadecimal values representing the "
"intensity of the red, green and blue components in a scale of 00-ff."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:1292
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>dcop</command> <option>knewsticker</"
"option> <option>KNewsTicker</option> <option>backgroundColor</option></"
"userinput>\n"
"                        #0030ff\n"
"                        <prompt>%</prompt>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: index.docbook:1296
#, no-c-format
msgid "highlightedColor"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1298
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Returns the currently configured highlight color as a string in the format "
"<quote>#rrggbb</quote>, where <quote>rr</quote>, <quote>gg</quote> and "
"<quote>bb</quote> are two-digit hexadecimal values representing the "
"intensity of the red, green and blue components in a scale of 00-ff."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:1304
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>dcop</command> <option>knewsticker</"
"option> <option>KNewsTicker</option> <option>highlightedColor</option></"
"userinput>\n"
"                        #000080\n"
"                        <prompt>%</prompt>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: index.docbook:1308
#, no-c-format
msgid "newsSources"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1310
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Returns the list of currently registered news sources. Note that this "
"returns all news sources, not just the selected ones. In the output, each "
"news source name will be printed on a line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:1314
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>dcop</command> <option>knewsticker</"
"option> <option>KNewsTicker</option> <option>newsSources</option></"
"userinput>\n"
"                        Freshmeat\n"
"                        GNOME News\n"
"                        dot.kde.org\n"
"                        Slashdot.org\n"
"                        <prompt>%</prompt>"
msgstr ""

